# Phase 15b probe — run once, deliberately, under the refetch protocol
# (not part of the normal offline pipeline).
#
# Purpose: verify Legislature XIX (19) is still the current legislature
# before trusting any Phase 15b predicate-discovery result — if a later
# legislature integer appears in the graph, Legislature XIX is no longer
# current and everything downstream (including senato_senatori.rq's own
# FILTER(?legislatura = 19)) would be querying a superseded legislature.
#
# Enumerates every distinct ?legislatura value reachable from a Senatore's
# ?mandato. If the highest integer value present is 19, with nothing
# beyond it, XIX is confirmed current.
#
# NOTE: an earlier draft of this probe used GROUP BY/COUNT/SUM(IF(...))
# to also report per-legislature current-mandate counts in one query —
# that aggregate form gets HTTP 403 from this endpoint (confirmed live;
# not a generic block, since this plain SELECT DISTINCT and the existing
# tools/queries/senato_senatori.rq both succeed against the same
# endpoint/User-Agent). Simplified to what the endpoint actually accepts;
# the plain distinct-value enumeration is sufficient to answer "is a later
# legislature present" without needing per-legislature counts.

PREFIX osr: <http://dati.senato.it/osr/>

SELECT DISTINCT ?legislatura
WHERE {
  ?senatore a osr:Senatore ;
            osr:mandato ?mandato .
  ?mandato osr:legislatura ?legislatura .
}
ORDER BY ?legislatura
